<http://data.silknow.org/object/a2ef1424-aa3a-32dc-9214-224d0cfed9ed>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Middle East, Textile; Panel, silk-embroidered cotton, packed design of quatrefoil medallions and crosses on yellow ground, Azerbaijan or NW Iran, 1750-1775"@en , "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning on the diagonal and cross stitch.\nYellow ground with a series of off-set quatrefoil shapes in blue with a faded pink lozenge centre or faded pink with a light blue lozenge centre in alternate rows.  Each is framed by bifurcated bars in blue and formed by a small multi-coloured star form, so forming a broken lattice.\nEmbroidery threads: 2S silk; black, faded pink, light pink, green, light blue, dark blue, blue, yellow, turquoise."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/76a55c05-8d1d-3d4b-b309-9d1a6a0814ba> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/18e44d5b-d96a-3781-a26c-60c5be2f781c> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/69978f01-0033-3858-a903-f548a0b05819> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in surface darning on the diagonal and cross stitch.\nYellow ground with a series of off-set quatrefoil shapes in blue with a faded pink lozenge centre or faded pink with a light blue lozenge centre in alternate rows.  Each is framed by bifurcated bars in blue and formed by a small multi-coloured star form, so forming a broken lattice.\nEmbroidery threads: 2S silk; black, faded pink, light pink, green, light blue, dark blue, blue, yellow, turquoise."@en , "Middle East, Textile; Panel, silk-embroidered cotton, packed design of quatrefoil medallions and crosses on yellow ground, Azerbaijan or NW Iran, 1750-1775"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/a2ef1424-aa3a-32dc-9214-224d0cfed9ed/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/a2ef1424-aa3a-32dc-9214-224d0cfed9ed/dimension/1> ;
